From 23cd9a2e6318102f836534d37333cdeaa588b93b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:13:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] perf(control-plane): open SQLite databases in WAL mode

The control plane opens the registry and the dedup key store on the
same database file. In the default rollback-journal mode an open read
on one connection blocked commits on the other one until the
five-second busy timeout expired, and the commit then failed with
"database is locked".

All control-plane stores (registry, dedup keys, tasks, audit log and
outbox) now open their connections through
forgemesh.controlplane.sqlite.connect, which enables WAL and foreign
key enforcement. synchronous stays FULL, because NORMAL lets a
committed write that was already acknowledged disappear after a power
loss in WAL mode; the busy timeout stays at the five-second default
of sqlite3.connect.
